{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>In the morning, and He will know, etc.</b> Now is a time of drunkenness for us, and it is not proper to appear before Him — and he intended to delay, perhaps they would retract (ibid.)." "<b>In the morning YHWH will make known those who are His.</b> For the Levitical service." "<b>And the holy one.</b> For the priesthood." "<b>And bring near.</b> them <b>to him;</b> and the Targum proves thus: ״וִיקָרֵב לָקֳדָמוֹהִי״, ״יְקָרֵב לְשִׁמּוּשֵׁיהּ״; and so one says <b>in the morning</b> — Moses said to them: The Holy One, blessed be He, set boundaries in His world; can you turn morning into evening? So too can you nullify this, as it is said, ״וַיְהִי עֶרֶב וַיְהִי בֹקֶר וַיַּבְדֵּל״ (Genesis 1) — likewise ״וַיִּבָּדֵל אַהֲרֹן לְהַקְדִּישׁוֹ״ etc. (I Chronicles 23)."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {3 "Reading וּמִ״אַ ('and so one says') as introducing a second interpretation; (שם) in comment 0 refers back to the same verse."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:11:13.298340182Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}